From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:50:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 097/117] drm/msm: signal completed hw fences without waiting
 for retire

Since commit 3c7a52217a8c ("drm/msm: Drop update_fences()") the IRQ
handler only advances the completed fence; the hw_fence of a submit, and
the scheduler fence attached to its BOs, is signalled only when
retire_submits() reaches the submit, and retire_submits() takes the
reservation lock of each BO of the submit before it moves to the next
one.

Completing a fence must not need a dma_resv lock: dma_fence_wait() may be
called with one held. The msm shrinker does exactly that (active_evict()
waits for the fences of a BO it holds locked), so under memory pressure a
reclaiming task that holds BO locks and the retire worker can end up
waiting on each other until each wait times out, BO after BO.

Signal the completed submits' fences from msm_gpu_retire() again, which
runs from the IRQ handler, the hangcheck timer and the recover worker:
after advancing the completed fence, walk the ring's submits under
submit_lock and signal them in order up to the first one that is not
done. retire_submits() still does the cleanup.

Problem analysis and approach by yzddmr6 (linux-sm8750 tree e11a25e13387,
"drm/msm: Signal completed hw fences from the irq handler", no
Signed-off-by); re-implemented.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
index 54093ce9b4c97..34ef145fb8e30 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -876,13 +876,43 @@ static void retire_worker(struct kthread_work *work)
 	retire_submits(gpu);
 }
 
-/* call from irq handler to schedule work to retire bo's */
+/*
+ * Signal the hw_fence of every submit the GPU has completed. This must not
+ * wait for retire_submits(), which takes the reservation lock of each BO of a
+ * submit: a dma_fence_wait() under such a lock (the shrinker evicting an
+ * active BO, for one) would otherwise wait for a fence that is only signalled
+ * once it lets go of the lock. Submits on a ring complete in order, so stop at
+ * the first one that is not done; dma_fence_is_signaled() signals a fence that
+ * msm_fence_signaled() reports complete. The fence lock nests in submit_lock.
+ */
+static void msm_gpu_signal_completed(struct msm_ringbuffer *ring)
+{
+	struct msm_gem_submit *submit;
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&ring->submit_lock, flags);
+	list_for_each_entry(submit, &ring->submits, node) {
+		if (!dma_fence_is_signaled(submit->hw_fence))
+			break;
+	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ring->submit_lock, flags);
+}
+
+/*
+ * call from irq handler to signal completed fences and schedule work to
+ * retire bo's
+ */
 void msm_gpu_retire(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	int i;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < gpu->nr_rings; i++)
-		msm_update_fence(gpu->rb[i]->fctx, gpu->rb[i]->memptrs->fence);
+	for (i = 0; i < gpu->nr_rings; i++) {
+		struct msm_ringbuffer *ring = gpu->rb[i];
+
+		/* the completed fence first, unconditionally */
+		msm_update_fence(ring->fctx, ring->memptrs->fence);
+		msm_gpu_signal_completed(ring);
+	}
 
 	kthread_queue_work(gpu->worker, &gpu->retire_work);
 }
